# Circutor CVM-C5.
# Converted automatically from the Omni Console device library (OmniCoreST); see ATTRIBUTION.md.
# Not verified against the manufacturer's documentation.
# Corrections are welcome (CONTRIBUTING.md). Remove @x_status once this table has been checked against the manual.
# | Circutor CVM-C5 — Panel-Mount 3-Phase Power Analyzer (Modbus RTU RS-485)
# | 
# | Source: circutor-cvm-c5-instruction-manual.pdf (section 4.7.2, pp. 43-45)
# | Models: CVM-C5-ITF-485, CVM-C5-MC-485, CVM-C5-mV-485
# | Protocol: Modbus RTU, FC03/04 read, FC10 write, 8N1 default
# | Baud: 1200/2400/4800/9600/19200 bps (configurable; default 9600)
# | All MODBUS addresses are hexadecimal in source; converted to decimal here.
# | All parameters are s32 (2 consecutive registers, 32-bit signed).
# | Scaling: V×10, current in mA, Hz×10, PF×100, THD %×10.
# | Energy: u32 in Wh or varh. Two tariffs (T1/T2); T1 addr listed here.
# | Active tariff selection: FC10 write to register 5000 (0=T1, 1=T2).
@mbmap=1
@vendor=Circutor
@model=CVM-C5
@vendor_website=circutor.com
@description=3-phase panel power analyzer, Modbus RTU RS-485 (CVM-C5-xxx-485). FC03/04 read, FC10 write. Phase V(×10)/I(mA)/P/Q/PF per phase (s32) at addr 0-28; inductive/capacitive reactive at 380-396; 3-phase totals at 30-66; THD at 48-58. Energy Wh/varh (u32) T1 at 60-102, T2 at 108-122. Tariff select FC10 at 5000.
@source=Omni Console device library (OmniCoreST), modbus-library/circutor-cvm-c5.toml; Source: circutor-cvm-c5-instruction-manual.pdf (section 4.7.2, pp. 43-45). Not verified against the manufacturer's documentation
